   3039  fc8a							; TAIL-jmp LoadLevel (bugs.md #29 Class B, 2026-10-11). The old
   3040  fc8a							; `jsr LoadLevel / zeros / rts` left FOUR jsr slots live when LoadLevel
   3041  fc8a							; reached `jsr EnterRoom`: CheckEnemyHit/timer death paths ran
   3042  fc8a							; main->jsr CEH->jmp LoseLife->jsr ReloadLevel->jsr LoadLevel->
   3043  fc8a							; jsr EnterRoom at SP=$F7, so the return address sat on $F6/$F7
   3044  fc8a							; (BombX/BombTimer), EnterRoomB2's `sta BombTimer` zeroed the pushed
   3045  fc8a							; PCH, and ReturnPad's rts popped ($00<<8|BombX)+1 = $009A -> ZP
   3046  fc8a							; executed as code -> $F008 pad -> GameStart REBOOT to title (the
   3047  fc8a							; SIM_EXIT=down f265 296-line crash frame + the title-264 family).
   3048  fc8a							; With the tail-jmp the slot count drops by one: EnterRoom's return
   3049  fc8a							; lands on $F8/$F9 (stack-only cells) on every death path.
   3050  fc8a							; The old post-code (vy/JetPower zeros + rts) was unreachable; DELETED
   3051  fc8a							; 2026-10-16 (intro music) — the $FDD8 blast-tramp pin below absorbs the
   3052  fc8a							; shift, so the twins stay put. DropArm zeroes vyLo/vyHi/PlayerYSub itself
   3053  fc8a							; (JetPower=4 stays through the drop-in flutter — identical to the .LLStay
   3054  fc8a							; path). LoseLife's `sec` still runs (DropArm's rts pops the jsr ReloadLevel
   3055  fc8a							; slot back into LoseLife).
   3056  fc8a		       4c 84 f5 	      jmp	LoadLevel
